[[0,275752,0,15,5,10,"2015-07-14T21:43:38","Kinther","",[],"<p>It's already happening -- users are downvoating comments and submissions they don't agree with rather than openly discussing why they disagree with them. In order for this site to function as a platform for freedom of speech without censorship, downvoats must not become something that users have infinite amounts of.</p>\n<p>I would like to suggest that downvoats should detract from your total CCP count. If you downvoat a comment, you lose a CCP. This would make users more careful about downvoating content or comments, and only downvoat if content or comments add nothing of value. It also would force users to engage the community rather than getting their 100 CCP and then going back to lurking. As a third benefit to this proposal, it would also mitigate downvoat brigades.</p>\n<p>Thoughts?</p>","Downvoats should not be something to silence opposing thoughts","","ideasforvoat"],[1,964274,0,1,0,1,"2015-07-14T21:47:46","Random_____User1","",[],"<p>Umm maybe have a downlvoat limit per day. </p>"],[2,964420,964274,2,0,2,"2015-07-14T21:51:02","Kinther","",[],"<p>The goal is to keep the community from becoming a race to 100CCP and then people downvoat. Those that have the power shouldn't abuse it, right? Limiting daily downvoats would be a good middle ground. 100CCP = 1 downvoat, 200CCP = 2 downvoats?</p>"],[1,964476,0,10,1,9,"2015-07-14T21:52:48","Frenchgeek","",[],"<p>...<br />\nI just thought of something : downvoats are a form of speech.</p>\n<p>Therefore, limiting downvoat mean limiting your freesom of speech. Which mean you are suggesting implementing the exact opposite of your goal in order to achieve it. \r</p>\n<p>Welp, either I need more coffee or my mind is even weirder than I thought...</p>"],[2,964608,964476,1,0,1,"2015-07-14T21:55:36","Kinther","",[],"<p>Downvoats are also a way to silence speech. Disagreeing with someone is fine. Debating with them is good, because it makes people come to terms why they agree or disagree with something. Simply downvoating without discourse is what I'd like to avoid. Would you be happy if someone downvoated all your comments on a vendetta because you said something they disagreed with?</p>"],[3,964888,964608,1,0,1,"2015-07-14T22:02:30","Frenchgeek","",[],"<p>I wouldn't care one bit. And I think that's the only healthy way to deal with IKP.</p>\n<p>( When I joined reddit originally, my goal was simply to have interesting content. Then when I started participating, I somehow found myself caring too much about karma.</p>\n<p>Took me a while to unlearn it, I admit. )</p>"],[3,968851,964608,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T23:44:13","CrowTRobot","",[],"<p>You aren't silenced if you get downvoated. The comment still exists, and anyone who cares to read it can open it and do so. </p>\n<p>If people are simply down voating shit in order to fall in line with everyone else, then that's a community or psychological problem. And that problem is considerably broader in scope than what we're looking at here.</p>"],[4,969259,968851,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T23:56:30","Kinther","",[],"<p>I suppose you're right. The underlying problem is that people will downvoat things they disagree with and not bother with discourse. My initial thought here was that limiting downvoats would stop voting brigades or stall them, but you're probably right -- they'll do it anyway and find a way around it if they really want to do it.</p>"],[1,965388,0,3,0,3,"2015-07-14T22:14:53","Canaduck","",[],"<p>Maybe if you're getting downvoated, the problem isn't in the number of downvoats, but in what you decided to post.</p>"],[2,965590,965388,1,0,1,"2015-07-14T22:20:02","Kinther","",[],"<p>This is not reflective of what I've posted or some issue with being downvoated, this was a platform wide idea I wanted feedback on. Yeah, if you post spam, you should be downvoated. If you post an interesting article or point out some relevant part of it in a discussion and are downvoated without any discourse, that seems to go against what Voat is trying to accomplish.</p>"],[3,965839,965590,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T22:26:18","Canaduck","[e]",[],"<p>I agree with most of what you said, but (for brevity) maybe someone has seen it before (on voat), or disagrees and doesn't want to waste their finger dexterity (there are lot of people like this). </p>\n<p>If I thought I was being unfairly downvoated then I would message the subverse moderator or an admin if its a site wide issue. Then I'd be able to decide if its an issue with me or the site.</p>"],[1,966355,0,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T22:38:12","microlyfe","",[],"<p>The community gains nothing from downvoating unpopular opinions. Comments that go against Voat's majority opinions will weaken hiveminds, ruin &quot;circlejerks&quot;, and spark debates.</p>"],[1,968781,0,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T23:42:22","Crackmacs","",[],"<p>I like the way downvoates are currently implemented and see no reason to change it. </p>"],[1,969594,0,1,0,1,"2015-07-15T00:05:42","Rutcrex","",[],"<p>I just came here to write exactly this. An idea would be to have 4 buttons: <strong>more visability - less visability</strong> and <strong>I agree - I don't agree</strong></p>"],[2,972033,969594,1,0,1,"2015-07-15T01:09:31","Murky42","",[],"<p>It will clutter the interface a bit but I like it anyway!</p>"]]
[[0,275753,0,7,0,7,"2015-07-14T21:43:52","OTL_","",[],"<p>I have a decent sized comment (883 characters in 188 words) and it keeps telling me that I'm &quot;doing this too fast&quot; and need to wait 30 seconds before trying again, which I've done multiple times. Is there a restriction based on CCP? My comments aren't too fast either so I highly doubt it's that.</p>","Is there a character limit for comments?","","AskVoat"],[1,964161,0,10,0,10,"2015-07-14T21:45:10","granmasboi","[e]",[],"<p></p>\n<p></p>\n<p>Don't think so</p>\n<p>Edit: Doubled the a's</p>"],[2,964359,964161,1,0,1,"2015-07-14T21:49:41","l-emmerdeur","",[],"<p>You didnt try hard enough. At some number it begins giving you the &quot;youre trying to do that too fast. please wait 30 seconds&quot; message.</p>\n<p>I dunno where it happened but I started at somewhere in the 100,000s characters and was not letting me submit</p>"],[3,964548,964359,1,0,1,"2015-07-14T21:54:36","granmasboi","",[],"<p>Okay. I'll try harder. Sorry. </p>"],[2,964363,964161,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T21:49:46","Gaterbate","",[],"<p>That's only 1367 characters with spaces, you should add more</p>"],[3,964523,964363,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T21:53:54","granmasboi","[e]",[],"<p>Just doubled it. I wonder if it's a word limit. </p>\n<p>Edit: I tried to double it again, and it didn't accept the edit. :/ </p>"],[2,965251,964161,5,0,5,"2015-07-14T22:10:53","OTL_","",[],"<p>Thank you for your hard work, sir! Hope your grandma is doing well?</p>"],[3,965490,965251,2,0,2,"2015-07-14T22:17:24","granmasboi","",[],"<p>Dude, she's awesome! Thanks for asking :) </p>"],[1,964542,0,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T21:54:21","avaimedia","",[],"<p>I had the same problem with the &quot;30 seconds&quot; message. I was giving someone a syntax example so my comment included characters like square brackets and a plus symbol. I tried removing those characters and typing them out instead (like you see here in this comment) and then it accepted my comment.</p>"],[2,966625,964542,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T22:44:21","Curiousmower","[e]",[],"<ul>\n<li>[] - </li>\n</ul>\n<p>edit: it works for me...except the plus symbol turns into that dot</p>"],[3,997175,966625,1,0,1,"2015-07-15T14:43:35","avaimedia","[e]",[],"<p>Actually &quot;[I think I wrote something more like this] + and then this&quot; and some words.</p>\n<p>Edit: That worked. Not sure what the problem was before, then.</p>"],[4,1007156,997175,1,0,1,"2015-07-15T19:05:44","Curiousmower","",[],"<p>Hmm maybe it was just a weird bug.</p>"],[1,964896,0,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T22:02:48","japr","",[],"<p>I have gotten this from both longer private messages and comments, and also from shorter private messages and comments. Shorter comments seem to rarely run into the issue, but it seems to me an occasional site-wide bug right now.</p>"],[1,966583,0,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T22:43:25","IAm_Chewbacca","",[],"<p>I don't know about for comments, but I know that posts have a character limit of 10,000</p>"],[1,966586,0,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T22:43:26","JH1010","",[],"<p>883 characters...</p>\n<p></p>\n<p>Seems fine.</p>"],[1,967031,0,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T22:55:49","jakeinator21","",[],"<p>I tried to do one with 524,288 characters and got the same message about commenting too often. </p>"],[1,968004,0,0,0,0,"2015-07-14T23:20:54","moo3001","",[],"<p>Ok 5000ish chars-\r\</p>"]]
